From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Robin <robinei@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 18:11:55 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm/i915/wm: Don't use DDR DVFS on CHV

EXPERIMENT, not for upstream.

With the DDR DVFS watermark level active, i915 clears FORCE_DDR_HIGH_FREQ
and the Punit may change the DDR frequency whenever the display FIFO
allows it. On a GPD Win 1 the DSI picture intermittently loses alignment
in light, bursty games but not in constantly GPU-heavy ones, which would
fit frequency switches. Limit CHV to the PM2/PM5 levels so the driver
forces DDR to the high frequency. Costs some idle power.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/i9xx_wm.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/i9xx_wm.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/i9xx_wm.c
index 86d1c9f..c0e11fe 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/i9xx_wm.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/i9xx_wm.c
@@ -1504,7 +1504,11 @@ static void vlv_setup_wm_latency(struct intel_display *display)
 		display->wm.pri_latency[VLV_WM_LEVEL_PM5] = 12;
 		display->wm.pri_latency[VLV_WM_LEVEL_DDR_DVFS] = 33;
 
-		display->wm.num_levels = VLV_WM_LEVEL_DDR_DVFS + 1;
+		/*
+		 * EXPERIMENT: never allow DDR DVFS for the display; the Punit
+		 * then keeps DDR at the high frequency (FORCE_DDR_HIGH_FREQ).
+		 */
+		display->wm.num_levels = VLV_WM_LEVEL_PM5 + 1;
 	}
 }
 
